From fc827ace40176250a777236fb8aace1f1cc17870 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Youngteac Hong <susukang98@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 20 Jul 2026 21:00:09 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Upload dropped files into the current folder, not Home
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Drag-and-drop / import-pick uploads always created documents at the
workspace root, ignoring the folder the list was viewing, while the
manual "New …" path correctly honored it.

The upload queue never threaded folderId: startBatch called enqueue
with only workspaceId, UploadItem had no folderId field, and the
getOrCreateDoc payload omitted it — so createWorkspaceDocument (which
already accepts folderId) received undefined and the backend filed the
doc at the root.

Thread folderId from the viewing folder through enqueue -> UploadItem
-> getOrCreateDoc so dropped and picked files land where the user is,
matching the manual create path.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
